From a1b98abdd1c9abf1b13aa8a5307e86e944189b66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 11:21:53 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 37/87] kosmickrisp: correct 2D array aliasing of 3D images

Metal cannot view a 3D texture as a 2D array, so a 3D image created with
VK_IMAGE_CREATE_2D_ARRAY_COMPATIBLE_BIT also allocates an auxiliary 2D array
texture over the same heap memory. That alias was described with the 3D
image's own mip count, but Metal bounds a 2D array texture's mip count with
max(width, height) while a 3D texture's bound also considers depth. A 3D
image deeper than it is wide therefore asked for more levels than the alias
can hold and Metal aborted the process while binding image memory: a 7x7x12
image with the four level chain Mesa allocates for it reports "requests 4
mipmap levels, but the dimensions (7, 7, 1) can only support a maxiumum of 3
levels". Every OpenGL CTS copy_image functional case that builds a
GL_TEXTURE_3D hit this.

Bound the alias to the levels a 2D array of its width and height may carry,
and refuse a 2D or 2D array view naming a level the alias omits instead of
letting Metal reject the texture view.

The alias also does not describe a mipmapped 3D image's slices: Metal packs a
2D array layer's whole mip chain together, so the alias' layer stride stops
matching the image's z slice stride as soon as the image has a second level.
Metal has its own way to name a 3D texture's z slice as a render target, so
render every 3D image through its own texture and select the slice with the
render pass depth plane rather than with an alias layer. A view that also
changes the format reinterprets that texture as a 3D view instead of taking a
2D array view of the alias, so a mutable-format render reaches the same slice.

Add a KosmicKrisp test that binds a 7x7x12 image with one level and with the
full four level chain, draws a distinct color into every z slice of every
level a 2D array view can name, and reads every level back, both through a
matching view and through a format-reinterpreting one.

(cherry picked from commit e4769c2686948b47a4f74f608acb6fa071c8e502)
